	"descriptionMarkdown": "I found a blueprint that did some very compact circuitry, but I was dissatisfied with it in operation. The machine would spend ages filling up with ingredients, make a single craft, and empty itself because another, higher, quality just became available.\n\nMy take on the issue introduces hysteresis to the system: It waits for 10x crafts' worth of ingredients to become available, and crafts until the available ingredients dry up.\n\nThis is a one-way implementation; uncommon crafts get overridden by rare crafts for example, but not the other way around. This way your legendary crafts are maximised in productivity!\n\nThe blueprints themselves use bob's adjustable inserters, because that's how I play my game, but with a tiny bit of reverse engineering you should be able to use the circuitry itself even without the mod (hopefully, unless the game disallows the inserters being pasted in the game)\n\nThe book contains Assembler, EM Plant and Foundry versions, and the circuitry itself with no machinery (only inserters, because some are needed to be wired up for the logic to work)\n\nI highly recommend the blueprint for anyone interested in learning advanced circuitry as well. I extensively document my works through combinator comments and blueprint descriptions (as far as the character limit allows anyway).\n\nEnjoy!\n\nUPDATE: The max items to upcycle didn't have the quality filter applied properly, I might fix this in the future, but for fear of braking the blueprint I won't do it right now.",
